  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nThis is a scoped structural result: **no new \u03ba, no construction.** It adds only `research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p109/`. The selected record, `upstream/` and all frozen pins are unchanged.\n\n#1419's extension lemma makes P112 minus X rigid whenever X lies inside a frame of P112. For three-line punctures that leaves **198688 of the 227920 triples**, which fall into **19 FRAME0-stabiliser orbits**: 18 contain an odd pair, and one (1792 triples) is pairwise orthogonal but lies in no P112 frame. This PR proves rigidity on all 19 with #1425's per-unit method. Each orbit representative gets:\n\n- a pivot frame passing #1212's (I3) and (I4) with gluing, with 18 to 24 complete classes;\n- #1399's Lemma 9 connectivity for the 5\u201329 lines outside complete classes;\n- a new DRUP refutation of #1212's zero-pattern CNF for (I2) zero exclusion, of 1595 to 2945 lemmas.\n\n**Consequence.** With #1419, **every P109 unit** (P112 minus any three lines) is rigid. Every decoder with exactly eight costly terms in the E-graph model there has cst \u2265 61, which is #968's 72 \u2212 p at p = 11.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `python3 -I -B research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p109/verify.py` runs 25 exact checks in about 15 s, standard library only. It is self-contained:\n  - **Census.** It recomputes the orbit census of triples and the inside-a-frame split, 24 orbits = 5 covered + 19 open, and checks that the units hit each open orbit once.\n  - **Per unit.** It checks the pivot conditions, builds each CNF itself and replays all 19 proofs from `PROOFS.json.gz` (658 KB) with its own two-watched-literal RUP checker. The SHA256 of each decompressed proof and each CNF is pinned.\n  - **Controls.** The gauge pattern satisfies each CNF. Each proof fails without the \"some entry vanishes\" clause. An empty-clause-only proof is rejected.\n- **Cross-checks, run once:**\n  - #1212's own `rup_check` (head `57099cb5`) accepts all 19 proofs, with identical lemma counts, and rejects every one without the zero clause.\n  - A census written independently by OpenAI Codex, from a specification only, matches the orbit table exactly: every (size, odd pairs, inside-a-frame) triple, plus |H| = 344064.\n  - A read-only adversarial review, also by Codex, found no soundness gap. It covered the CNF families, the lemma hypotheses, subgroup coverage and the RUP checker, including 10000 random fuzz formulas.\n- `make_proof.py` (python-sat 1.9.dev15, Glucose 4.1) regenerates `UNITS.json` and `PROOFS.json.gz` byte-identically in about 4 s.\n- Passes on Python 3.10, 3.12 and 3.14. `scripts/research_package.py`: the metadata check and the Python 3.12 registered replay pass. `test_research_*` passes.\n\n## Not checked or not covered\n\n- **Inherited steps**, cited and not re-derived:\n  - #1212's Lemmas 5\u20136, \u00a77 and transport;\n  - #1399's Lemma 9;\n  - #1419's Lemma 10 and its P104 inputs, for the 29232 covered triples.\n\n  All of these PRs are open. #968's (F6) is inherited. Attainment of 61 is not checked. There has been no independent human review.\n- **P108 and deeper.** 168 open orbits at |X| = 4. The same pipeline passes on all of them; #1474 packages that result. Nine or more costly terms are not covered.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- **Task / scope:** `complex-masked-decoder` (scope key `2a6f2c726b78f9ae7d26`), refined to #1425's open next question. Track complex-mechanisms, priority revision 2. The task was assigned by the donor as \"the open thread\", so no reroll.\n- **Heads:** base `410026dc5513b87db92ae98571d1d5984c69a983`. Cites #1212 `57099cb5`, #1399 `4e1ba3a1`, #1419 `81b8997b` and #1425 `4b707c22`. It imports nothing from them.\n- **Claim:** https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1411#discussioncomment-18912490\n- **Overlap:** none on P109 or P108 beyond my own claim. Refreshed at 01:11Z (826 open PRs and 162 discussions, complete pagination).\n\n## Credit\n\n- **burntout76 / Brett Halligan (#1212):** the theorem, (E), the CNF families of Lemmas 4/8, the pivot reduction, Lemmas 5\u20136, \u00a77 and the transport.\n- **themilkman216 (#968):** the floor.\n- **DreamingOfClouds (#717):** the E-graph model.\n\nSubstantial AI assistance: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code (proof, verifier, CNF/RUP reimplementation, write-up); OpenAI Codex (independent census and read-only review). Submitted by the account holder. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
